messages:
maya: Heads-up — onboarding for WellPath hitting sustained 429s on mobile hybrid app during SDK startup. Spike correlates with app open/rotate.

 devops-bot: alert -> rate_limit_spike customer=wellpath key=sk_live_zzz window=2026-03-22T08:45Z peak=410r/s :warning:

 rene: Any chance they're calling SDK.init on every visibilitychange or orientation event? Hybrid webviews are notorious for that.

 maya: Yep. They call init on visibilitychange to refresh ephemeral tokens and they're also using Background Sync to replay queued requests.

 omar: That's a classic fanout: visibilitychange x background-sync replay x short TTL ephemeral tokens = handshake storm. Also saw lots of OPTIONS preflights in the edge logs.

 kai: Reproduced in our device lab: rotate -> visibilitychange fires twice, init invoked twice, network flap -> background-sync retries queued POSTs, leading to 3-4x multiplier. If token TTL is 20-30s and each spawn mints a new token it's worse.

 maya: Captured failing POST from device (429):

 -----
 POST /v1/sessions HTTP/1.1
 Host: api.redwood.example
 Authorization: Bearer eph_live_xyz
 Content-Type: application/json
 {"client":"wellpath-android","sdk":"web-1.9.2"}
 -----

 omar: Immediate mitigation recommended to customer: 1) debounce SDK.init on visibilitychange (e.g., 500ms), 2) stop minting ephemeral per-visibility — mint on server and reuse for short window (5m), 3) disable Background Sync for onboarding rollout.

 kai: SDK-side improvements we advised: respect Retry-After, exponential backoff with jitter, and telemetry counters for 429s so CS can triage quickly. We'll add a guard to prevent concurrent inits in the next release.

 maya: They applied debounce + server-issued token reuse and toggled Background Sync off. Rate dropped from ~410r/s to ~22r/s in ~8 minutes and onboarding completed. :white_check_mark:

 rene: Follow-ups: add KB note for hybrid webview gotcha, update browser SDK docs about service workers/background-sync, and add a short renewal risk flag for accounts that show this pattern during ramp.

 maya: I'll file the KB, open a tiny docs PR, and log this in Gainsight for renewals. Scheduling a 20-min enablement call with their eng lead tomorrow.

 omar: Can you include the debounce snippet in the KB? e.g.:

 -----
 let initTimeout = null;
 document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => {
   clearTimeout(initTimeout);
   initTimeout = setTimeout(() => {
     if (!sdk.isInitialized()) sdk.init();
   }, 500);
 });
 -----

 maya: Adding now. Closing loop once PR and Gainsight entry are in. :thumbsup:
